{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>But the man who is pure, etc.</b> One must know why the verse did not write the punishment for one who neglects the Paschal offering in its time until now — and not when it wrote the commandment of the Paschal offering. According to what they disagreed about this matter (Pesachim 93b), and this is their language: The Sages taught — he is liable for the first and liable for the second, these are the words of Rabbi; Rabbi Natan says: he is liable for the first and exempt for the second; Rabbi Ḥanina ben Akiva says: even for the first he is not liable unless he did not perform the second. And they said there in Pesachim that all three of them derived from one verse — one should look there. From this it follows that for each of the opinions the Scripture left it to say up to here, for each of the opinions according to its way — something we would not have heard thus if it had commanded it in its [original] place."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:06:57.823307347Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}